WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.444
Alice stood outside the house, unsure what to do next.

2
00:00:07.445 --> 00:00:12.138
Suddenly a footman in uniform ran out of the woods.

3
00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:18.035
The footman had a face like a fish.

4
00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:25.823
He knocked on the door, which was answered by another footman.

5
00:00:25.824 --> 00:00:30.907
This one had a round face and eyes like a frog.

6
00:00:30.908 --> 00:00:35.620
Alice noticed that both wore curly powdered wigs.

7
00:00:35.621 --> 00:00:43.290
"I wonder what's going to happen." Alice crept closer so she could listen.

8
00:00:43.291 --> 00:00:48.212
The Fish Footman was holding a letter almost as big as himself.

9
00:00:48.213 --> 00:00:51.219
He handed it to the Frog Footman.

10
00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:54.794
"From the Queen," the Fish Footman said.

11
00:00:54.795 --> 00:01:00.226
"An invitation for the Duchess to play croquet."

12
00:01:00.227 --> 00:01:04.285
"This must be the Duchess' house," Alice said to herself.

13
00:01:04.286 --> 00:01:08.724
"I wonder if she's the Duchess that the White Rabbit was talking about."

14
00:01:08.725 --> 00:01:14.472
The two footmen bowed low, tangling their curls together.

15
00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:24.454
Alice laughed so hard that she ran into the woods so they wouldn't hear her.

16
00:01:24.455 --> 00:01:28.460
When she peeped out again, the Fish Footman was gone.

17
00:01:28.461 --> 00:01:40.364
The Frog Footman was sitting on the ground, staring at the sky.

18
00:01:40.365 --> 00:01:45.255
Alice went to the door of the house and knocked quietly.

19
00:01:45.256 --> 00:01:49.490
"There's no point in knocking," the Frog Footman said.

20
00:01:49.491 --> 00:01:53.531
"First, I'm out here with you, so I can't open the door.

21
00:01:53.532 --> 00:02:00.608
Second, they're making so much noise inside, no one can hear you."

22
00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:05.196
Alice put her ear on the door to listen.

23
00:02:05.197 --> 00:02:07.565
The Frog Footman was right.

24
00:02:07.566 --> 00:02:11.212
There was a constant howling and sneezing.

25
00:02:11.213 --> 00:02:15.694
Every once in a while came a great crash.

26
00:02:15.695 --> 00:02:20.408
"That sounds like dishes breaking!" Alice said to the Frog Footman.

27
00:02:20.409 --> 00:02:23.437
"But how will I get inside?"

28
00:02:23.438 --> 00:02:26.356
The Frog Footman had no idea.

29
00:02:26.357 --> 00:02:30.393
"I'm going to sit out here all day," he said.

30
00:02:30.394 --> 00:02:34.659
Just then the door opened, and a plate flew outside.

31
00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:40.117
It almost hit the Frog Footman before smashing against a tree.

32
00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:45.906
He continued to sit as if nothing had happened.

33
00:02:45.907 --> 00:02:51.487
"Or maybe I'll sit here until tomorrow," he said quietly.

34
00:02:51.488 --> 00:02:57.955
Alice decided to open the door herself.

35
00:02:57.956 --> 00:03:02.853
The door led right into the kitchen, which was full of smoke.

36
00:03:02.854 --> 00:03:06.650
The Duchess sat on a stool, feeding a baby.

37
00:03:06.651 --> 00:03:11.892
The Cook was leaning over the fire, stirring a pot of soup.

38
00:03:11.893 --> 00:03:19.269
Alice began to sneeze.

39
00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:23.090
"There's too much pepper in that soup!" she cried.

40
00:03:23.091 --> 00:03:29.267
The baby took turns sneezing and howling.

41
00:03:29.268 --> 00:03:35.931
The Duchess sneezed once in a while, but the Cook didn't sneeze at all.

42
00:03:35.932 --> 00:03:40.619
A cat was lying on the hearth and grinning from ear to ear.

43
00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.712
It didn't sneeze either.

44
00:03:44.713 --> 00:03:48.721
"I've never seen a cat grin like that," Alice said.

45
00:03:48.722 --> 00:03:53.064
"Then you haven't been paying attention," the Duchess said.

46
00:03:53.065 --> 00:04:00.705
"All cats know how to grin, but this Cheshire Cat is especially good at it. Pig!"

47
00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:05.919
The Duchess said this last word so loudly that Alice jumped.

48
00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.503
Then she realized the Duchess was speaking to the baby.

49
00:04:10.504 --> 00:04:14.904
The baby had tiny eyes and a nose like a snout.

50
00:04:14.905 --> 00:04:23.406
Before Alice could say a word, the Cook started throwing things.

51
00:04:23.407 --> 00:04:27.021
"Watch what you're doing!" Alice said.

52
00:04:27.022 --> 00:04:29.388
"You're going to hurt the baby!"

53
00:04:29.389 --> 00:04:32.316
The Duchess tossed the baby to Alice.

54
00:04:32.317 --> 00:04:35.536
"Here, you can feed the baby if you like.

55
00:04:35.537 --> 00:04:40.533
I must get ready to play croquet with the Queen."

56
00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:45.798
And with that, the Duchess hurried from the room.

57
00:04:45.799 --> 00:04:52.978
Alice tried to hold onto the wiggling baby while the Cheshire Cat simply grinned.

